{"reference_id": 1, "content": "Love and Theft is the second studio album by Eric Gunderson and Stephen Barker Liles in the American country music duo Love and Theft. It was released on July 24, 2012 via RCA Nashville. The album includes the number 1 single \"Angel Eyes.\" The album's second single, \"Runnin' Out of Air,\" was released to country radio in November 2012. The album's third single, \"If You Ever Get Lonely\", was released to country radio on June 3, 2013. This song was originally recorded by John Waite on his 2011 album \"Rough & Tumble\"."}
